=== layout: section

# First Division\: Meiosis 1


=== layout: one-panel

# Stages of Meiosis I

@body

- Division in meiosis I occurs in four phases
  - Prophase I
  - Metaphase I
  - Anaphase I
  - Telophase I and cytokinesis


=== layout: big-image

@image

![Prophase I and metaphase I.](assets/lect06c-meiosis/meiosis_prophase_metaphase_i.svg)

@caption

Prophase I and metaphase I.

=== layout: one-panel

# Meiosis Prophase I Terminology

@body

- [*Homologous*]{underline=true} – Chromosomes with the same genes in the same order, but possibly different versions of those genes.
- [*Homologous chromosomes*]{underline=true} – chromosome pairs (one from each parent) that are [similar]{color=red} in length, gene position, and centromere location
- [*Sister chromatids*]{underline=true} – two [identical]{color=red} copies of a single replicated chromosome, joined at the centromere until they separate.
- [*Synapsis*]{underline=true} – Side-by-side pairing of homologous chromosomes.
- [*Crossing over*]{underline=true} – Swapping of matching DNA pieces between non-sister chromatids of homologous chromosomes, creating new gene combinations.
- [*Chiasmata*]{underline=true} – the physical links between homologous chromosomes at crossover sites, holding them together until they separate


=== layout: section

# Prophase I is incredibly complex (more than Prophase II) and is divided into six (6) sub-stages


=== layout: two-panels

# Stages of Prophase I

@left

![Slide image 4](assets/lect06c-meiosis/image_004.png)

@right

- 1. Leptotene
  - Chromosomes condense and become visible
  - Thread-like [chromomeres]{underline=true} appear
- 2. Zygotene
  - Homologous chromosomes begin pairing (synapsis)
  - Many points of contact form


=== layout: two-panels

# Stages of Prophase I

@left

- Pachytene: homologs exchange DNA
- 3. Early Pachytene
  - Pairing complete; crossing over begins
- 4. Late Pachytene
  - Chromosomes shorten and thicken
  - Sister chromatids become visible

@right

![Slide image 5](assets/lect06c-meiosis/image_005.png)


